`_codes_to_group_indices` builds `N` empty lists, then scans the 1D `codes` array and appends each position `n` to `groups[g]` whenever `g >= 0`. For `groupby_bins`, `BinGrouper.factorize` gets those codes from `pd.cut` using bins `[-2, 0, 3, 5, 10]` with right-closed intervals, so the bins are `(-2,0]`, `(0,3]`, `(3,5]`, `(5,10]`. Applying that to `score=[-4,-1,0,2,6,7,11]` gives codes `[-1,0,0,1,3,3,-1]`, so positions 1 and 2 go to group 0, position 3 to group 1, group 2 stays empty, and positions 4 and 5 go to group 3.

## Answer
{"group_indices":[[1,2],[3],[],[4,5]]}
